          "id": "code-ml-03-1-ch03_1_scratch",
          "title": "First-Principles: Fisher Scoring Logistic MLE, Bias 1/n & Batas Cramér-Rao",
          "language": "python",
          "filename": "03_1_fisher_scoring_crlb.py",
          "code": "import numpy as np\n\n# 1) Verifikasi bias MLE varians (1/n) vs koreksi Bessel (1/(n-1))\nrng = np.random.default_rng(42)\ntrue_var = 4.0\nn_small = 10\nn_trials = 4000\nsamples = rng.normal(loc=5.0, scale=np.sqrt(true_var), size=(n_trials, n_small))\n\nmle_vars = np.var(samples, axis=1, ddof=0)\nunbiased_vars = np.var(samples, axis=1, ddof=1)\nprint(f\"True Variance          : {true_var:.4f}\")\nprint(f\"E[sigma^2_MLE] (ddof=0): {mle_vars.mean():.4f} (Teori (n-1)/n * var = {true_var * (n_small - 1) / n_small:.4f})\")\nprint(f\"E[s^2_Bessel]  (ddof=1): {unbiased_vars.mean():.4f}\")\n\n# 2) Fisher Scoring (Newton-Raphson) untuk Logistic Regression MLE + Cramer-Rao SE\ndef fit_logistic_fisher(X, y, max_iter=25, tol=1e-9):\n    w = np.zeros(X.shape[1], dtype=float)\n    for _ in range(max_iter):\n        z = np.clip(X @ w, -30.0, 30.0)\n        p = 1.0 / (1.0 + np.exp(-z))\n        score = X.T @ (y - p)                       # Gradien log-likelihood\n        W = p * (1.0 - p)\n        fisher_info = (X.T * W) @ X + 1e-10 * np.eye(X.shape[1])\n        step = np.linalg.solve(fisher_info, score)\n        w = w + step\n        if np.linalg.norm(step) < tol:\n            break\n    z = np.clip(X @ w, -30.0, 30.0)\n    p = 1.0 / (1.0 + np.exp(-z))\n    fisher_info = (X.T * (p * (1.0 - p))) @ X\n    crlb_se = np.sqrt(np.diag(np.linalg.inv(fisher_info)))\n    return w, crlb_se\n\ntrue_w = np.array([-0.5, 1.2, -0.8])\nn_obs = 600\nX_base = np.column_stack([np.ones(n_obs), rng.normal(0.0, 1.0, size=(n_obs, 2))])\np_true = 1.0 / (1.0 + np.exp(-(X_base @ true_w)))\n\n# Simulasi Monte Carlo 300 ulangan untuk membandingkan SE empiris vs batas Cramer-Rao\nmc_estimates = np.zeros((300, 3))\nfor t in range(300):\n    y_sim = rng.binomial(1, p_true)\n    mc_estimates[t], _ = fit_logistic_fisher(X_base, y_sim)\n\nw_hat, crlb_se_hat = fit_logistic_fisher(X_base, rng.binomial(1, p_true))\n# Fisher Information teoretis pada parameter sejati\nfisher_true = (X_base.T * (p_true * (1.0 - p_true))) @ X_base\ncrlb_se_true = np.sqrt(np.diag(np.linalg.inv(fisher_true)))\n\nprint(\"--- Perbandingan Standard Error MLE vs Batas Bawah Cramer-Rao (n=600) ---\")\nfor j, name in enumerate([\"w0 (intercept)\", \"w1\", \"w2\"]):\n    emp_se = mc_estimates[:, j].std(ddof=1)\n    print(f\"  {name:14s} | True={true_w[j]:+.2f} | EmpSE={emp_se:.4f} | CRLB(true)={crlb_se_true[j]:.4f} | PlugInSE={crlb_se_hat[j]:.4f}\")",
          "expectedOutput": "True Variance          : 4.0000\nE[sigma^2_MLE] (ddof=0): 3.6329 (Teori (n-1)/n * var = 3.6000)\nE[s^2_Bessel]  (ddof=1): 4.0365\n--- Perbandingan Standard Error MLE vs Batas Bawah Cramer-Rao (n=600) ---\n  w0 (intercept) | True=-0.50 | EmpSE=0.1060 | CRLB(true)=0.1014 | PlugInSE=0.1000\n  w1             | True=+1.20 | EmpSE=0.1156 | CRLB(true)=0.1189 | PlugInSE=0.1197\n  w2             | True=-0.80 | EmpSE=0.1150 | CRLB(true)=0.1121 | PlugInSE=0.1092",
          "actualOutput": "True Variance          : 4.0000\nE[sigma^2_MLE] (ddof=0): 3.6329 (Teori (n-1)/n * var = 3.6000)\nE[s^2_Bessel]  (ddof=1): 4.0365\n--- Perbandingan Standard Error MLE vs Batas Bawah Cramer-Rao (n=600) ---\n  w0 (intercept) | True=-0.50 | EmpSE=0.1060 | CRLB(true)=0.1014 | PlugInSE=0.1000\n  w1             | True=+1.20 | EmpSE=0.1156 | CRLB(true)=0.1189 | PlugInSE=0.1197\n  w2             | True=-0.80 | EmpSE=0.1150 | CRLB(true)=0.1121 | PlugInSE=0.1092",
          "explanation": "Memverifikasi bias MLE varians 1/n secara Monte Carlo dan mencocokkan SE empiris regresi logistik terhadap batas bawah Cramér-Rao.",
