          "solution": "```python\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef asymmetric_reject_band(probs, cost_fp: float, cost_fn: float, cost_reject: float) -> dict:\n    p = np.asarray(probs, dtype=float)\n    tau_low = cost_reject / cost_fn\n    tau_high = 1.0 - (cost_reject / cost_fp)\n    actions = []\n    expected_risk = 0.0\n    if tau_low < tau_high:\n        for pi in p:\n            if pi < tau_low:\n                actions.append(0)\n                expected_risk += pi * cost_fn\n            elif pi > tau_high:\n                actions.append(1)\n                expected_risk += (1.0 - pi) * cost_fp\n            else:\n                actions.append(-1)\n                expected_risk += cost_reject\n    else:\n        tau_elkan = cost_fp / (cost_fp + cost_fn)\n        for pi in p:\n            if pi >= tau_elkan:\n                actions.append(1)\n                expected_risk += (1.0 - pi) * cost_fp\n            else:\n                actions.append(0)\n                expected_risk += pi * cost_fn\n    return {\n        \"tau_low\": round(float(tau_low), 4),\n        \"tau_high\": round(float(tau_high), 4),\n        \"actions\": actions,\n        \"expected_risk\": round(float(expected_risk), 2),\n    }\n\nres = asymmetric_reject_band([0.02, 0.15, 0.65, 0.90], cost_fp=50.0, cost_fn=500.0, cost_reject=20.0)\nprint(res)\n```"
